hadiths[27]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1210","Abū Rāshid Ḥibrānī (may Allāh have mercy on him) narrates: \I came into the presence of Sayyiduna ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿAmr (may Allāh be pleased with them both) and requested: 'Narrate to me a hadith that you heard from the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him).' He handed me a scroll and said: 'This is the scroll that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) wrote for me.' I looked at it and found therein: 'Indeed"","" Sayyiduna Abū Bakr al-Ṣiddīq (may Allāh be pleased with him) asked the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""O Messenger of Allāh! Teach me a supplication that I may recite in the morning and evening.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""O Abū Bakr"","" recite: 'O Allāh"","" Originator of the heavens and the earth"","" Knower of the unseen and the seen"","" Lord and Sovereign of all things. I seek refuge in You from the evil of my own self"","" from the evil of Shayṭān and his shirk"","" and from committing any wrong against my own soul or causing harm to any Muslim.'\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"","" Hadith: 1210; Arabic Hadith: 1210*"""""
"1211","Sayyiduna Ḥudhayfah (may Allāh be pleased with him) narrates that when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to sleep, he would say: \In Your name"","" O Allāh"","" I die and I live.\"" And when he awoke from sleep"","" he would say: \""All praise is due to Allāh"","" Who gave us life after causing us to die"","" and unto Him is the resurrection.\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"","" Hadith: 1211; Arabic Hadith: 1211*"""""
"1212","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allāh be pleased with him) narrates that when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came to his bed, he would recite this supplication: \All praise is due to Allāh"","" Who fed us"","" gave us drink"","" sufficed us"","" and provided us with shelter — and how many are those who have none to suffice them or provide them shelter.\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"","" Hadith: 1212; Arabic Hadith: 1212*"""""
"1213","Sayyiduna Jābir (may Allāh be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) would never sleep without first reciting Sūrah al-Sajdah and Sūrah al-Mulk. Abū Zubayr says: \These two sūrahs possess a merit exceeding that of every other sūrah of the Noble Qur'ān by seventy virtues. Whoever recites both of them shall have seventy good deeds recorded for him"","" seventy ranks elevated for him"","" and seventy sins erased through them.\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"","" Hadith: 1213; Arabic Hadith: 1213*"""""
"1214","Sayyiduna ʿAbdullāh (may Allāh be pleased with him) narrates, saying: \Sleep at the time of dhikr (remembrance) comes from Shayṭān. If you wish"","" you may test this. When any one of you goes to his bed and intends to sleep"","" let him remember Allāh"","" the Mighty and Majestic.\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"","" Hadith: 1214; Arabic Hadith: 1214*"""""
"1215","Sayyiduna Jābir (may Allāh be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) would not sleep until he had completed the recitation of Sūrah al-Mulk and Alīm Sajdah (Sūrah al-Sajdah).\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad, Hadith: 1215; Arabic Hadith: 1215*"
"1216","Sayyiduna Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When any one of you lies down on his bed"","" let him shake out the inner garment of his lower garment and dust off his bed with it"","" for he does not know what may have settled on it after he left it. And it is fitting that he lie on his right side and recite this supplication: 'In Your name"","" O Allāh"","" I have placed my side (on this bed). So if You take my soul"","" have mercy upon it"","" and if You release it"","" then protect it in the manner in which You protect the righteous among Your servants.'\"" Or he said: \""…in the manner in which You protect Your righteous servants.\""\n\n*Al-Adab al-Mufrad"","" Hadith: 1216; Arabic Hadith: 1216*"""""
"1217","It is narrated by Sayyiduna Barā' ibn 'Āzib (may Allāh be pleased with them both) that when the Prophet (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) would go to his bed, he would lie on his right side and then recite this supplication: \O Allāh"","" I have directed my face toward You"","" and I have entrusted my soul to You"","" and I have placed my reliance upon You"","" out of hope for Your bounty and fear of Your punishment. There is no place of refuge and no sanctuary besides You. I have believed in the Book which You have revealed and in the Prophet whom You have sent.\"" Then he (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) said: \""Whoever recites these words (with faith and conviction) during the night and then passes away that same night"","" his death shall be upon the natural disposition (fiṭrah).\"""""""
"1218","It is narrated by Sayyiduna Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him) that when the Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) would lie down on his bed, he would recite: \O Allāh"","" Lord of the heavens and the earth"","" Sovereign of all things"","" Splitter of the grain and the seed"","" Revealer of the Tawrāh"","" the Injīl"","" and the Qur'ān. I seek refuge in You from the evil of every evil thing whose forelock is in Your Hand. You are the First—nothing is before You. You are the Last—nothing is after You. You are the Manifest—nothing is above You. You are the Hidden—nothing is beyond You. Settle my debt and enrich me"","" so that I may be free from want.\"""""""
"1219","It is narrated by Sayyiduna Barā' ibn 'Āzib (may Allāh be pleased with them both) that when the Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) would come to his bed, he would lie on his right side and then recite: \O Allāh"","" I have entrusted my soul to You"","" I have directed my face toward You"","" I have consigned my affair to You"","" and I have placed my reliance upon You in all my matters"","" out of hope in You and fear of You. There is no place of refuge and no sanctuary for me besides You. I have believed in the Book which You have revealed and in the Messenger whom You have sent.\"" The Messenger of Allāh (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) said: \""Whoever recites these words and then passes away that same night"","" his death shall have come upon the natural disposition (fiṭrah).\"""""""
"1220","It is narrated by Sayyiduna Jābir (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said: When a person enters his house or goes to his bed, an angel and a devil hasten toward him. The angel says: \End your affair with goodness"",""\"" and the devil says: \""End your affair with evil.\"" If he then praises and remembers Allāh"","" the angel repels the devil and guards him throughout the night. When he awakens"","" the angel and the devil again hasten toward him"","" and the same exchange takes place. If he remembers Allāh and says: \""All praise belongs to the One who returned my soul to me after death and did not cause it to die in its sleep. All praise belongs to the One who keeps the heavens and the earth from moving out of their places—if they were to move"","" who could hold them after Him? Indeed"","" He is the Most Forgiving"","" the Most Pardoning. All praise belongs to the One who keeps the heavens from falling upon the earth except by His permission—indeed"","" He is the Most Compassionate"","" the Most Merciful.\"" If he passes away (in that state)"","" he dies upon martyrdom"","" and if he rises and performs ṣalāh"","" it is a prayer of great virtue."""""
"1221","It is narrated by Sayyiduna Barā' (may Allāh be pleased with him) that when the Prophet (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) intended to sleep, he would place his hand beneath his right cheek and recite: \O Allāh"","" protect me from the punishment of the Day on which You will raise Your servants.\"" It is also narrated from Sayyiduna Barā' through another chain in a similar manner."""""
"1222","It is narrated by Sayyiduna 'Abdullāh ibn 'Amr (may Allāh be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) said: \Whoever adheres to two practices shall certainly enter Paradise. They are both easy"","" and those who act upon them are few.\"" It was asked: \""O Messenger of Allāh"","" what are they?\"" He (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) said: \""After every ṣalāh"","" one should recite 'Allāhu Akbar' ten times"","" 'Alḥamdulillāh' ten times"","" and 'Subḥānallāh' ten times. That totals one hundred and fifty upon the tongue and one thousand five hundred on the Scale.\"" I (the narrator) saw the Prophet (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) counting them on his hand. And when he went to his bed"","" he would recite 'Subḥānallāh' thirty-three times"","" 'Alḥamdulillāh' thirty-three times"","" and 'Allāhu Akbar' thirty-four times—that is one hundred upon the tongue and one thousand on the Scale. \""Which of you commits two hundred and fifty sins in a day and night?\"" It was asked: \""O Messenger of Allāh"","" how can a person not act upon this?\"" He said: \""The devil comes to one of you during his ṣalāh and reminds him of various worldly matters"","" so that he does not remember these glorifications.\"""""""
"1223","It is narrated by Sayyiduna Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him) that the Prophet (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) said: \When any of you goes to his bed"","" let him take the inner part of his lower garment and dust the bed with it"","" and recite 'Bismillāh"",""' for he does not know what has come upon the bed after he left it. Then"","" when he intends to lie down"","" let him lie on his right side and recite: 'O my Lord"","" pure is Your name. By Your name I lay myself down"","" and by Your grace I shall rise. If You take my soul"","" then forgive it; and if You release it"","" then guard it as You guard Your righteous servants.'\"""""""
"1224","It is narrated by Rabi'ah ibn Ka'b (may Allāh be pleased with him) that I used to spend the night at the door of the Prophet's (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) house so that I could provide him with water for wuḍū' and other needs. I would hear him at length during the night reciting \Sami' Allāhu li-man ḥamidah\"" and at length reciting \""Alḥamdulillāhi Rabbil-'Ālamīn.\"""""""
"1225","It is narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn 'Abbās (may Allāh be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) said: \Whoever falls asleep while his hands are greasy (with food) and does not wash them"","" and then something (harmful) bites him"","" let him blame none but himself.\"""""""
"1226","It is narrated by Sayyiduna Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him) that the Prophet (ṣallallāhu 'alayhi wa sallam) said: \Whoever sleeps with greasy hands and then something (harmful) bites him"","" let him blame none but himself.\"""""""
"1227","Sayyidunā Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh (may Allāh be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \At night"","" close the doors"","" tie the mouths of the water-skins"","" overturn the vessels or cover them"","" and extinguish the lamps. For indeed"","" Shayṭān does not open a closed door"","" nor does he untie a water-skin"","" nor does he uncover a covered vessel. And verily"","" the mouse is a wicked creature that sets people's houses on fire.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"","" Hadith: 1227 | Arabic Hadith: 1227"""""
"1228","Sayyidunā Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allāh be pleased with them both) narrates. He said: A mouse came and began pulling the wick of the lamp. A girl went to stop it, but the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Leave it.\"" So the mouse brought the wick and placed it upon the mat on which he was reclining. An area of the mat the size of a dirham was burned. The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) then said: \""When you go to sleep"","" extinguish your lamps"","" for indeed"","" Shayṭān instructs such creatures in such matters"","" and they set you on fire.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"","" Hadith: 1228 | Arabic Hadith: 1228"""""
"1229","Abū Saʿīd (may Allāh be pleased with him) narrates. He said: One night the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was awake. He suddenly saw a mouse climbing onto the roof carrying a wick so as to set the house on fire. Thereupon, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) cursed it and declared its killing permissible even within the sacred precinct (Ḥaram).\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad, Hadith: 1229 | Arabic Hadith: 1229"
"1230","Sayyidunā Ibn ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with them both) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \Do not leave fire burning in your houses when you go to sleep.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"","" Hadith: 1230 | Arabic Hadith: 1230"""""
"1231","Sayyidunā ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with him) said: \Indeed"","" fire is an enemy"","" so beware of it.\"" Consequently"","" Sayyidunā Ibn ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with them both) was especially vigilant regarding fire in his house and would extinguish it before going to sleep.\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"","" Hadith: 1231 | Arabic Hadith: 1231"""""
"1232","Sayyidunā Ibn ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with them both) narrates that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: \Do not leave fire burning in your houses (at night)"","" for it is an enemy.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"","" Hadith: 1232 | Arabic Hadith: 1232"""""
"1233","Sayyidunā Abū Mūsā (may Allāh be pleased with him) narrates. He said: One night, a house in Madīnah al-Ṭayyibah was set ablaze along with its inhabitants. When this was mentioned to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), he said: \This fire is your enemy. Therefore"","" when you go to sleep"","" extinguish it.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"","" Hadith: 1233 | Arabic Hadith: 1233"""""
"1234","Sayyidunā Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allāh be pleased with him) narrates that when rain would descend, he would say: \O girl! Take out my saddle and my clothes.\"" And he would recite: \""And We sent down from the sky blessed water.\"" (Qāf"","" 50:9)\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"","" Hadith: 1234 | Arabic Hadith: 1234"""""
"1235","Sayyidunā Ibn ʿAbbās (may Allāh be pleased with them both) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded that refuse be hung inside the house.\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad, Hadith: 1235 | Arabic Hadith: 1235"
"1236","Sayyidunā Jābir ibn ʿAbdullāh (may Allāh be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \When night falls and stillness prevails"","" reduce your movement"","" for none among you knows which of Allāh's creatures the Almighty spreads abroad. Close the doors"","" tie the mouths of the water-skins"","" cover the vessels"","" and extinguish the lamps.\""\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"","" Hadith: 1236 | Arabic Hadith: 1236"""""
